  "title": "Replacing overhead lines with underground cables in Finland",
  "summary": "The electricity distribution operator Elenia invests in substantial underground cabling aiming for 75% by 2028 to meet outage requirements and adapt to climate change impacts such as extreme weather events. This enhances energy supply security and cost savings, supported by collaboration with telecommunications companies and technology integration. This case study considers a Finnish example of replacing overhead lines with underground cabling. The same strategy is also applied in other European countries. Elenia is the second largest electricity distribution system operator in Finland.",
